WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.500
This is Hudson, as you can see he’s pretty excited about being at the beach today.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.200
However, there is a bylaw in place for how the beaches in the Waimakariri are used

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.640
and it includes some pretty key rules for us dog owners.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.780
Dogs are welcome at most beaches in the Waimakariri

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.300
however they’re not allowed around the Ashley-Rakahuri Estuary and Wetlands

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.220
that’s to safeguard the local bird habitat.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.320
Dogs also aren’t allowed between the surf flags or within 50 metres of the flags.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.200
And around horses on the beach, dogs must be under effective control

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.300
If they can’t be controlled by your voice then they must be put on a leash.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.400
So that’s it in a nutshell, it’s really simple

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.320
and as always make sure you bring plenty of these to clean up after your furry friend.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.880
We’ve all got a part to play in preserving our beaches and estuary.

